    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields.java` (the first step in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, which already binds the body and collects field errors into `OwnerFieldsInvalidException` \u2192 handled as 400):\n\n- Added a check: when `registrationDate` is present and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`, add `\"registrationDate\"` to the error list, triggering the existing 400 response.\n- Added the `java.time.LocalDate` import and updated the class javadoc.\n\nThis fits the project's existing convention \u2014 `registrationDate` is optional (defaults to the server date when omitted via `BuildOwner`/`BusinessDays`), so unspecified dates are unaffected; only a supplied future date is rejected. No new exception/handler/YAML was needed since the existing field-validation error path already returns 400.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` test (posting `2999-01-01`) now passes, and the full suite builds green.",
