    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change lands exactly where this codebase already puts owner field validation. `ValidateOwnerFields` is, by design, the single place that validates every field on the create body \u2014 it already handles both required fields (firstName, telephone) and optional-when-present fields (email, postcode). The new registrationDate check follows the established optional-field idiom precisely: null-guard, validate, `errors.add(...)` into the shared list, reported together via `OwnerFieldsInvalidException`. \n\n- Right unit: field-level validation belongs here, not in a separate step or in `BuildOwner`.\n- Not duplicated: reuses the existing `errors` accumulator and exception path.\n- Not a catch-all creeping in: this class's explicit purpose is to validate owner fields, so one more field is additive, not scope-expanding.\n- The Javadoc and inline comment were updated to match, consistent with the surrounding comment style (each optional field already carries an explanatory comment).\n\nNaturally idiomatic for a maintainer of this file.",
